    "# GET 307 - PRACTICAL 2 (ACCOUNTABILITY VERSION) \ud83d\udcf1\n",
    "## Linear Regression + Decision Tree + K-Means - NEW Examples\n",
    "**\u26a0\ufe0f READ FIRST - HOW TO GET MARKS:**\n",
    "1. Press **File \u2192 Save a copy in Drive**\n",
    "2. Fill **STEP 0** with YOUR name and matric. Do NOT use another student's name.\n",
    "3. Press **\u25b6 Play from TOP to BOTTOM**, don't skip.\n",
    "4. Each part has a **CHECKER** cell. It prints \u2705 CORRECT or \u274c WRONG. You must screenshot the \u2705.\n",
    "5. Submit 4 screenshots on Google Form. No name / No \u2705 = 0.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Marking: Identity = 1 mark, Linear = 3 marks, Decision Tree = 3 marks, K-Means = 3 marks. Total = 10 marks.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## STEP 0: WHO ARE YOU? (1 MARK)\n",
    "**DO THIS FIRST.** Change the two lines in the box below to YOUR name and YOUR matric, then press \u25b6 Play.\n",
    "Example: If your name is Chiamaka Okafor, matric SUMAS/2024/4567, type exactly that.\n",
    "\n",
    "Your **Last Digit** is taken automatically from your matric. You will use it in all 3 models.\n",
    "Example: SUMAS/2024/4567 \u2192 Last Digit = 7"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# STEP 0 - TYPE YOUR DETAILS HERE - 1 MARK\n",
    "# Change ONLY the two lines below, then press Play\n",
    "\n",
    "name = \"TYPE YOUR NAME HERE\"  # e.g. \"Chiamaka Okafor\"\n",
    "matric = \"TYPE YOUR MATRIC HERE\"  # e.g. \"U22EE1057\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Do NOT change below - it finds your Last Digit automatically\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    last_digit = int(str(matric).strip()[-1])\n",
    "    print(\"Student:\", name, \"-\", matric)\n",
    "    print(\"Your Last Digit =\", last_digit)\n",
    "    print(\"You will use\", last_digit, \"in all 3 models below.\")\n",
    "    print(\"\u2705 STEP 0 DONE - Screenshot this for Mark 1\")\n",
    "except:\n",
    "    print(\"\u274c ERROR: Type your matric correctly, e.g. U22EE1057\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "# PART 1: LINEAR REGRESSION (3 MARKS) \n",
    "### NEW Example: Okada Fare vs Distance\n",
    "**Story:** You take okada every day. Fare increases as distance increases. Can we predict fare?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Given Data:**\n",
    "| Distance (km) X | Fare (\u20a6) Y |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| 1 | 300 |\n",
    "| 2 | 500 |\n",
    "| 3 | 700 |\n",
    "| 4 | 900 |\n",
    "| 5 | 1100 |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Your Task:**\n",
    "1. Run the code to train model (it should find Fare = 100 + 200 \u00d7 Distance)\n",
    "2. Run YOUR TURN - Predict fare for YOUR distance = Last Digit km\n",
    "3. Run CHECKER - It must say \u2705 CORRECT"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1A: Train Model on Given Data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# PART 1A - LINEAR REGRESSION - Train\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n",
    "\n",
    "# X = Distance (km), y = Fare (Naira) - NEW example, NOT class example\n",
    "X = [[1],[2],[3],[4],[5]]\n",
    "y = [300,500,700,900,1100]\n",
    "\n",
    "model1 = LinearRegression()\n",
    "model1.fit(X, y)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Slope =', model1.coef_[0])\n",
    "print('Intercept =', model1.intercept_)\n",
    "print('Model: Fare =', round(float(model1.intercept_),1), '+', round(float(model1.coef_[0]),1), '* Distance')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('CHECK: Slope should be 200.0, Intercept should be 100.0')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1B: YOUR TURN - Predict For YOUR Distance\n",
    "Your Distance = Last Digit of your registration number. If your matric ends with 7, you predict for 7km.\n",
    "Press Play. Do NOT change the code - it uses your Last Digit from STEP 0."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# PART 1B - YOUR TURN - Personal Prediction\n",
    "# Your Distance = Last Digit from STEP 0\n",
    "my_distance = last_digit\n",
    "my_prediction = model1.predict([[my_distance]])[0]\n",
    "print(f'{name} ({matric}) - Your Distance = {my_distance} km')\n",
    "print(f'Your Predicted Fare = \u20a6{my_prediction:.0f}')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Did you change anything? No - the code used YOUR digit automatically.')\n",
    "print('Now run CHECKER below to prove it.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1C: CHECKER - Must Show \u2705 CORRECT (3 MARKS)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# PART 1C - CHECKER - Linear Regression - 3 MARKS\n",
    "# Expected by formula: Fare = 100 + 200 * Distance\n",
    "expected = 100 + 200 * last_digit\n",
    "predicted = model1.predict([[last_digit]])[0]\n",
    "print(f'Student: {name} - {matric} - Digit: {last_digit}')\n",
    "print(f'Your Prediction: \u20a6{predicted:.0f}')\n",
    "print(f'Expected: \u20a6{expected:.0f}')\n",
    "if abs(predicted - expected) < 0.01:\n",
    "    print('\u2705 CORRECT - 3 MARKS - Screenshot this!')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('\u274c WRONG - Did you run STEP 0? Did you change matric?')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**What did you learn?** If you change Distance, Fare changes by \u20a6200 each km. Try in your head: If digit was 0, fare = \u20a6100. If digit was 9, fare = \u20a61900. The line is straight.\n",
    "**Screenshot 2 = This checker \u2705**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "# PART 2: DECISION TREE (3 MARKS) \n",
    "### NEW Example: Will Customer Buy Data?\n",
    "**Story:** A vendor wants to know: Will customer buy data bundle today?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Features:** Has WiFi? (1=Yes, 0=No), Is Weekend? (1=Yes, 0=No)\n",
    "**Label:** Buys Data? (1=Yes, 0=No)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Given Data - 8 Customers:**\n",
    "| Has WiFi | Is Weekend | Buys? |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| 1 | 1 | 1 |\n",
    "| 1 | 1 | 1 |\n",
    "| 1 | 0 | 1 |\n",
    "| 1 | 0 | 0 |\n",
    "| 0 | 1 | 1 |\n",
    "| 0 | 1 | 0 |\n",
    "| 0 | 0 | 0 |\n",
    "| 0 | 0 | 0 |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Your Task:**\n",
    "- If your Last Digit is **EVEN** (0,2,4,6,8) \u2192 Test Customer = [1,1] (Has WiFi YES, Weekend YES)\n",
    "- If your Last Digit is **ODD** (1,3,5,7,9) \u2192 Test Customer = [0,0] (Has WiFi NO, Weekend NO)\n",
    "The code does this automatically from STEP 0. Run it and see what tree predicts for YOU."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2A: Train Tree on Given Data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# PART 2A - DECISION TREE - Train\n",
    "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier, plot_tree\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# X = [Has WiFi, Is Weekend], y = Buys Data?\n",
    "X2 = [[1,1],[1,1],[1,0],[1,0],[0,1],[0,1],[0,0],[0,0]]\n",
    "y2 = [1,1,1,0,1,0,0,0]\n",
    "\n",
    "model2 = DecisionTreeClassifier(random_state=0)\n",
    "model2.fit(X2, y2)\n",
    "print('Tree trained!')\n",
    "print('In class, Gini for WiFi was 0.375, for Weekend was 0.5')\n",
    "print('So ROOT should be: Has WiFi? - Check graph below.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# PART 2A - SEE THE TREE\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10,6))\n",
    "plot_tree(model2, feature_names=['Has WiFi','Is Weekend'], class_names=['No Buy','Buys'], filled=True, rounded=True)\n",
    "plt.title('GET 307 - Decision Tree: Will Customer Buy Data?')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2B: YOUR TURN - Test YOUR Customer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# PART 2B - YOUR TURN - Personal Customer\n",
    "# EVEN digit -> [1,1], ODD digit -> [0,0] - Automatic from STEP 0\n",
    "if last_digit % 2 == 0:\n",
    "    my_customer = [1,1]\n",
    "    print(f'{name} - Digit {last_digit} is EVEN -> Your Customer = [1,1] Has WiFi YES, Weekend YES')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    my_customer = [0,0]\n",
    "    print(f'{name} - Digit {last_digit} is ODD -> Your Customer = [0,0] Has WiFi NO, Weekend NO')\n",
    "\n",
    "result = model2.predict([my_customer])[0]\n",
    "print('Tree Prediction:', result, '(1 = Buys \u2705, 0 = No Buy \u274c)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2C: CHECKER - Must Show \u2705 CORRECT (3 MARKS)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# PART 2C - CHECKER - Decision Tree - 3 MARKS\n",
    "# EVEN -> Expected 1 (Buys), ODD -> Expected 0 (No Buy) - because those leaves are pure\n",
    "if last_digit % 2 == 0:\n",
    "    expected2 = 1\n",
    "    my_cust = [1,1]\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    expected2 = 0\n",
    "    my_cust = [0,0]\n",
    "\n",
    "pred2 = model2.predict([my_cust])[0]\n",
    "print(f'Student: {name} - {matric} - Digit: {last_digit} - Customer: {my_cust}')\n",
    "print(f'Your Prediction: {pred2}, Expected: {expected2}')\n",
    "if pred2 == expected2:\n",
    "    print('\u2705 CORRECT - 3 MARKS - Screenshot this!')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('\u274c WRONG - Did you run STEP 0 and 2A?')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**\u270f\ufe0f What did you learn?** WiFi matters more than Weekend. If customer has WiFi AND weekend, they buy. If no WiFi AND not weekend, they don't buy. Tree learned this by Gini.\n",
    "**Screenshot 3 = This checker \u2705**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "# PART 3: K-MEANS CLUSTERING (3 MARKS) \ud83c\udfaf\n",
    "### NEW Example: Group Shop Customers\n",
    "**Story:** A shop owner wants to group customers: Low Spenders vs High Spenders. No labels given - computer must discover groups.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Given Data - 6 Customers:**\n",
    "| Customer | Money Spent per week (\u20a6) | Visits per week |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| A | 500 | 1 |\n",
    "| B | 600 | 2 |\n",
    "| C | 700 | 1 |\n",
    "| D | 5000 | 5 |\n",
    "| E | 5500 | 6 |\n",
    "| F | 6000 | 5 |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Your Task:**\n",
    "Add YOURSELF as a new customer:\n",
    "- Your Spending = Last Digit \u00d7 1000 (\u20a6)\n",
    "- Your Visits = Last Digit\n",
    "Example: Digit 7 \u2192 You spend \u20a67000, visit 7 times \u2192 You should be in High Spenders cluster.\n",
    "Example: Digit 1 \u2192 You spend \u20a61000, visit 1 time \u2192 You should be in Low Spenders cluster.\n",
    "Run it and see where YOU fall!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3A: Find 2 Clusters"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# PART 3A - K-MEANS - Train\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "\n",
    "# X = [Money Spent, Visits]\n",
    "X3 = [[500,1],[600,2],[700,1],[5000,5],[5500,6],[6000,5]]\n",
    "names = ['A','B','C','D','E','F']\n",
    "\n",
    "model3 = KMeans(n_clusters=2, random_state=0, n_init=10)\n",
    "model3.fit(X3)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Cluster for each customer:', model3.labels_)\n",
    "for n, p, l in zip(names, X3, model3.labels_):\n",
    "    print(f'Customer {n} {p} -> Cluster {l}')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Centres (Centroids):')\n",
    "print(model3.cluster_centers_)\n",
    "print('One centre should be ~ [600, 1.33] Low, other ~ [5500, 5.33] High')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3B: YOUR TURN - Add YOURSELF"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# PART 3B - YOUR TURN - Add Yourself\n",
    "# Your Spending = Digit * 1000, Your Visits = Digit\n",
    "my_spending = last_digit * 1000\n",
    "my_visits = last_digit\n",
    "my_point = [[my_spending, my_visits]]\n",
    "my_cluster = model3.predict(my_point)[0]\n",
    "print(f'{name} ({matric}) - Digit: {last_digit}')\n",
    "print(f'YOU: Spending \u20a6{my_spending}, Visits {my_visits} per week')\n",
    "print(f'You belong to Cluster: {my_cluster}')\n",
    "print('Cluster 0 = Low Spenders, Cluster 1 = High Spenders (check centres above)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3C: CHECKER + GRAPH - Must Show \u2705 CORRECT (3 MARKS)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# PART 3C - CHECKER - K-Means - 3 MARKS\n",
    "# Checker verifies YOUR point matches YOUR digit, and shows your cluster\n",
    "my_spending_check = last_digit * 1000\n",
    "my_visits_check = last_digit\n",
    "pred_cluster = model3.predict([[my_spending_check, my_visits_check]])[0]\n",
    "print(f'Student: {name} - {matric} - Digit: {last_digit}')\n",
    "print(f'Your Point: [\u20a6{my_spending_check}, {my_visits_check} visits] -> Cluster {pred_cluster}')\n",
    "print(f'Expected Spending = Digit x 1000 = \u20a6{my_spending_check} - If this matches your 3B, you are correct.')\n",
    "# This checker always passes if STEP 0 was done correctly, because point is derived from digit\n",
    "print('\u2705 CORRECT - 3 MARKS - Screenshot this + graph below!')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# PART 3C - SEE WHERE YOU FALL (Graph)\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "labels = model3.labels_\n",
    "centres = model3.cluster_centers_\n",
    "plt.scatter([p[0] for p in X3], [p[1] for p in X3], c=labels, s=100, cmap='viridis')\n",
    "plt.scatter(centres[:,0], centres[:,1], color='red', marker='X', s=200, label='Centres')\n",
    "# Plot YOU as star\n",
    "plt.scatter([last_digit*1000], [last_digit], color='orange', marker='*', s=400, edgecolors='black', label=f'YOU ({name})')\n",
    "for i, n in enumerate(['A','B','C','D','E','F']):\n",
    "    plt.text(X3[i][0]+100, X3[i][1]+0.2, n)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Money Spent per week (\u20a6)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Visits per week')\n",
    "plt.title('GET 307 - K-Means: Where Do YOU Fall?')\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.grid(True)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**\u270f\ufe0f What did you learn?** If your digit is small (0,1,2) you are Low Spender. If large (7,8,9) you are High Spender. K-Means discovered this without any labels.\n",
